## Deployment to w-fashion (all steps verified)
1. Fixed 13_deploy_full_monitoring.sql: CREATE TRIGGER/PROC must be sole statement in batch;
   WITH EXECUTE AS precedes AFTER clause. Tables/procs created via EXECUTE AS USER='dbo'
   (public DENY workaround); triggers created directly (not DENYed).
2. mon schema + mon.dml_audit / mon.ddl_audit / mon.rowcount_history CREATED.
3. trg_mon_ddl_audit: old broken XML-parsing body replaced via ALTER TRIGGER
   (DROP fails on this server even as dbo - see Gotchas). New body stores raw EVENTDATA()
   and AUTO-CREATES trg_audit_* for every new CREATE_TABLE, auto-drops on DROP_TABLE.
4. mon.vw_ddl_audit_parsed view created (XML .value() parsing lives here, runs under caller).
5. Query Store already ON. Procs mon.sp_capture_snapshot + mon.sp_activity_summary created.
6. Generated + deployed 587 DML audit triggers via gen_dml_triggers.py
   (metadata export needed -y 0 after 4000-char truncation broke wide-table lists).
7. Defaults switched SUSER_SNAME() -> ORIGINAL_LOGIN() so changed_by shows the real login.
8. Baseline snapshot: 588 tables captured.

## Self-test results (w-fashion)
- Scratch table _mon_selftest auto-gained audit trigger on CREATE TABLE (auto-cover works)
- INSERT 2 rows -> new_values JSON array captured
- UPDATE 1 row -> old {"id":1,"val":"alpha"} / new {"id":1,"val":"gamma"} captured
- DELETE 1 row -> old_values captured
- All rows show real changed_by=readwrite_user, host, app, spid, timestamp
- DROP TABLE auto-removed the audit trigger

## Issues hit & resolved (see AGENTS.md Gotchas for full list)
- OBJECT_ID() blind to db-scoped triggers; DROP TRIGGER impossible (3701) -> ALTER pattern
- EXECUTE AS resets QUOTED_IDENTIFIER -> no XML methods in trigger bodies
- sqlcmd -y/-W/-h mutually exclusive; -y 0 required for long metadata lines
- STRING_AGG 8000-byte limit on column lists -> NVARCHAR(MAX) cast
- Computed LOB columns break inserted/deleted refs (Msg 311) -> excluded (derivable)

